Equivalence Groups Found
└── Modbus client (TCP/RTU) for reading holding registers from a power meter
    ├── Candidates : pymodbus, minimalmodbus, modbus-tk
    ├── Used APIs  : ModbusTcpClient, connect, read_holding_registers, isError, 
    │   registers
    ├── Pitfalls   : minimalmodbus returns raw register lists directly and raises 
    │   exceptions on error instead of returning an object with isError(); minimalmodbus
    │   is primarily designed for serial (RTU) communication; TCP support is 
    │   limited/less idiomatic; modbus-tk uses a different master/query construction 
    │   pattern (query objects) rather than direct method calls like 
    │   read_holding_registers; unit/slave id parameter naming and defaults differ 
    │   across libraries; connection lifecycle management (connect/close) differs 
    │   between libraries
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── pymodbus is used here as a TCP Modbus master to connect to a device and read 
        holding registers, returning a response object with `.registers` and 
        `.isError()`. minimalmodbus and modbus-tk are both Modbus master libraries 
        capable of reading holding registers over TCP/RTU, making them functionally 
        equivalent at the protocol level. However their client APIs differ significantly
        from pymodbus's response-object pattern (minimalmodbus returns raw lists and 
        raises exceptions instead of an isError() flag; modbus-tk uses its own 
        master/query API), so a direct swap requires an adapter layer.

