context-manager object, not a long-lived handle that 
  ⚠ Remaining incompatibilities noted by connector LLM:
    - paho-mqtt's Client.connect() is a synchronous, fire-and-forget call that returns a
live client handle; aiomqtt only exposes connection scope via 'async with Client(...) as
client', so _default_client cannot synchronously return an already-connected client 
without restructuring as an async generator/context manager, which changes its call 
contract entirely.
    - TelemetryBridge.publish_reading calls self.client.publish(...) synchronously and 
reads a .rc attribute off the returned MQTTMessageInfo object; aiomqtt's publish() is a 
coroutine with no .rc-bearing return value, so publish_reading and publish_batch would 
both need to become 'async def' and be awaited by every caller -- this ripples through 
the entire public API and any external code that instantiates/uses TelemetryBridge 
synchronously.
    - The dependency-injection pattern (client=None constructor param, defaulting to 
_default_client(cfg)) assumes a synchronous, already-connected client object can simply 
be swapped in; injecting an aiomqtt client instead requires the caller to be inside an 
event loop and an 'async with' block at construction time, which a wrapper cannot 
retrofit onto synchronous call sites.
    - No wrapper can convert the whole synchronous call chain (constructor -> 
publish_reading -> publish_batch) into async without changing all downstream callers to 
use asyncio and 'await' -- this is a structural execution-model change, not a glue-code 
fix.

