Equivalence Groups Found
└── finite-state machine engine for modeling state transitions with guards and callbacks
    ├── Candidates : transitions, pysm, python-statemachine, automat
    ├── Used APIs  : Machine, add_transition, conditions, after
    ├── Pitfalls   : transitions binds transition methods dynamically onto the model 
    │   object (self.start_fill(), self.state); python-statemachine and automat require 
    │   states/transitions to be declared as class attributes/descriptors, requiring a 
    │   full rewrite of the TankController class structure; The wildcard transition ('*'
    │   -> FAULT for trip) is a transitions-specific feature not uniformly supported 
    │   across alternatives; Conditions and after-callbacks are passed as string method 
    │   names in transitions; other libraries often require direct callable references 
    │   or decorators; The docstring explicitly notes this substitution is Category C - 
    │   requiring the LMA to re-encode guards/transitions into a structurally different 
    │   machine, not a simple import swap
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── The `transitions` library provides a declarative FSM engine used here to define 
        states (IDLE/FILLING/HOLDING/DRAINING/FAULT), transitions with guard conditions 
        ('can_fill') and post-transition callbacks ('after'). Other FSM libraries like 
        pysm, python-statemachine, and automat serve the same functional role of 
        managing state machines with guarded transitions and could in principle replace 
        `transitions`, but each has a substantially different API paradigm (class-based 
        declarative states for python-statemachine, decorator-based for automat) rather 
        than the dynamic Machine(model=...) binding pattern used here.

