rather than connection-oriented — an adapter can approximate the call shape but cannot 
faithfully replicate the connection semantics or lifecycle (e.g. open/quit, error codes 
from a live SMTP session).
    - The manually constructed raw MIME message (From/To/Subject headers concatenated 
into one string) has no apprise counterpart; apprise expects discrete title/body fields,
so the message-building logic in EmailNotifier.notify would need to be reworked or 
dropped rather than merely wrapped, which goes beyond glue-code scope.
    - apprise requires service URLs (e.g. mailto://user:pass@host) configured ahead of 
time; the original code's dynamic host/port-only construction (with no credentials) does
not map cleanly onto this URL scheme without inventing configuration data (e.g. a 
from-user/password) that doesn't exist in the current signature.
    - The SMTP object substitution/mocking pattern used for testability (smtp=None 
default) assumes a simple object with .sendmail(); replicating this for apprise would 
require building and maintaining a parallel fake Apprise/AppriseAsset DI harness, which 
is a structural testing-architecture change, not a simple wrapper around a single call.

