    │   differ across libraries (unit= vs slaveaddress= vs slave=); pymodbus 3.x itself 
    │   changed its API significantly from 2.x (e.g., removed 'unit' kwarg in favor of 
    │   'slave'), so even within pymodbus versions migration care is needed
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── All four libraries provide Modbus master/client functionality capable of reading
        and writing holding registers over TCP (or serial in minimalmodbus's/modbus-tk's
        case), fulfilling the same functional role as pymodbus's ModbusTcpClient in this
        file. The code explicitly isolates the client behind a dependency-injected 
        factory (_default_client) and an IO wrapper class, making substitution 
        architecturally feasible at the call-site level.

